course: dictionary
lesson: 1635
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and a capital letter can be a clue. «A chihuahua and a Great Dane are the same species.» Here chihuahua means a small dog, because a Great Dane, another dog, is mentioned beside it. Read the words around the word to find which meaning fits.
explain: Chihuahua with a capital C is also a name. It is a large state in northern Mexico, and a city there. The dog is named after it. Ask yourself: is the sentence talking about a pet, or about a place on a map?
explain: In everyday life chihuahuas are popular pets, often carried in bags. They are lively and loyal, and they can be noisy and bossy for their size. A story might say a tiny chihuahua thinks it is big, and the words tell you the character's size and personality.
fact: A chihuahua is a very small breed of dog with big ears and big eyes.
fact: The chihuahua is the smallest dog breed in the world.
fact: Chihuahua with a capital letter is a large state in northern Mexico, and a city there.
fact: The dog is named after the Mexican state, which is where the breed is said to come from.
fact: «Dogs came from wolves tamed more than 15,000 years ago», and a chihuahua and a Great Dane are the same species.
exercise: «A chihuahua and a Great Dane are the same species.» What is a chihuahua in this sentence? | A kind of bird | *A very small breed of dog | A place in Mexico | A large cat
exercise: «Chihuahua is the largest state in northern Mexico.» What is Chihuahua in this sentence? | A famous dog show | A small village by the sea | A breed of dog | *A large state in northern Mexico
exercise: Chihuahuas are lively, loyal and can be noisy. What does loyal mean? | *Faithful, staying close to its owner | Afraid of water | Loud at night | Lazy and sleepy
test: «Dogs came from wolves tamed more than 15,000 years ago.» What does tamed mean? | Painted in bright colours | Lost in the snow | Hunted for food in the wild | *Made gentle enough to live with people
test: «Chihuahua is the largest state in Mexico.» What is Chihuahua in this sentence? | A type of sea | A dog breed | *A state in Mexico | A kind of food
exam: Jayden says a capital C can't matter, because a chihuahua is just a dog. Who is right? | Jayden is wrong, because chihuahuas are cats | *Jayden is wrong, because Chihuahua with a capital letter can be a place name | Jayden is right, capital letters never change a word's meaning | Jayden is right, because all dog names start with a capital letter
